If we look only at the immediate arithmetic, the structure has not changed: $\begin{aligned}
a_{\text{push}} &: (N_{\text{die}},N_{\text{live}}) = (1,5), \\
a_{\text{refrain}} &: (N_{\text{die}},N_{\text{live}}) = (5,1).\end{aligned}$ Yet the class no longer reacts as it did in the driver’s case. Most of those willing to turn the trolley are unwilling to push the man. The lecture now acquires its first real engine: comparative case variation.

